Restructured migration `0156` to avoid deadlocks on large deployments. The previous migration
used `ALTER COLUMN TYPE` which acquires `ACCESS EXCLUSIVE` and scans all rows to validate the
domain constraint — taking 40+ minutes on large databases and causing deadlocks with concurrent
workers. The migration now uses `ADD CONSTRAINT ... NOT VALID` (brief lock, no row scan) via
`SeparateDatabaseAndState`, and the SpGist index is created with `CONCURRENTLY`.
